From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:50:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 322/333] [ae-patch] Fix the Voice mode fix-check findings:
 stuck mic start, stale withdraw, done trimming

The fix check on the previous Voice mode patch found three problems its fixes introduced.

A mic start could get stuck: when the mic handle turned a start away (a take still finishing, a guard), nothing was reported, so the request flag stayed set and Voice mode sat on "Starting the mic" with no retry. The handle now reports whether a start began, tells Voice mode when it did not, and Voice mode treats a start that stays silent for 5 s as failed (one retry, then "Mic unavailable"). It also makes the start again when the mic is wanted before its own stop has finished.

A cancel flag left by a withdrawn start could make the next manual click on the mic button start a stream that was dropped at once. The flag is now cleared when the start ends either way, and a manual start ignores one left over.

On a multi-select card, trimming filler words ate the end of a label such as "Merge it". The whole remainder is now tried against the labels first and filler is trimmed only when nothing matched.

Also reverts a formatting-only change to the effort picker line in ChatPage so the patch touches only Voice mode lines.
